# What NOT to upload to Elastic Beanstalk.
#
# This file solves a specific trap. Without it, `eb deploy` packages whatever is
# committed to git - and frontend/dist/ is in .gitignore, because a build
# artifact does not belong in version control. The deploy would then arrive
# WITHOUT the React build, and Flask would serve its "API is running" fallback
# instead of your app.
#
# The moment .ebignore exists, EB stops consulting git entirely and packages the
# working directory, filtered by the rules below. So dist/ ships because it is
# not excluded here, while .env and your database still never leave the laptop.
#
# Anything listed below is EXCLUDED from the upload.

# --- secrets and local data: must never leave this machine ---
backend/.env
backend/.env.*
!backend/.env.example
backend/instance/

# --- installed packages: the server builds its own from requirements.txt ---
.venv/
backend/.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/

# --- frontend SOURCE is not needed; only the built output in dist/ is ---
frontend/src/
frontend/public/
frontend/index.html
frontend/vite.config.js
frontend/package.json
frontend/package-lock.json

# --- tests and dev tooling do not run on the server ---
backend/tests/
backend/pytest.ini
backend/requirements-dev.txt

# --- caches and build noise ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.vite/

# --- version control and editors ---
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
